{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED for exact clean pushed head a3bf832ef1fd8af73c00d4d9c3783628ab8c2f13 and primary cmd/gs artifact 514ab482d8b1f75d277d6b33e73ffdfc428dffdc.\n\nThe prior implementer-forgery finding is closed in the fold. TestMergeReceiptFromTheImplementerReachesNoUnrelatedTree reproduces the exact approval-for-spike / invented merge head / operator-owned docs victim / self-published docs successor probe: the supersession is now ineffective with reason \"actor may not supersede target\" and the victim remains live. validateMergeReceiptNow cuts the signer-written plan to the slash-delimited lineage of the artifact the independent reviewer named. Successor coverage, bystander rejection, legitimate same-lineage succession, unrelated-candidate protection, and the no-successor rule remain green.\n\nOne blocking pre-HEAD authority defect remains. mergeCommand validates approval independence and exact head but never checks that the actor selected by --as is the author of the approved implementation artifact. refuseUnreachableCrossAuthorRetirements only compares that actor with retirement-target authors and the approved path; for a normal same-path plan, a different bare participant passes the path-lineage branch. Git then commits. recordMergeSuccession finally produces a receipt signed by the wrong actor, which the fold correctly refuses, but this happens after HEAD has irreversibly moved.\n\nExact probe at this head: newWorkflowFixture creates operator's feature.txt artifact and reviewer's independent approval; reviewer then invokes gs merge --as reviewer. Expected: an error before HEAD moves. Actual: merge commit 47ac027a is created, then the command errors that predecessor c668238a remains live. The test fails: \"refused non-implementer merge moved HEAD ...\". This lets any participant with access to a public ratified approval consume its single-use merge authorization, move the target, and strand succession. It violates the original 82f20a1e condition to preserve pre-HEAD failure atomicity and the documented contract that the receipt is signed by the implementation author.\n\nRequired repair: before reserving/merging—or at latest before git commit—resolve the approval's named artifact statement and require the signing actor fingerprint to equal that artifact's actor, unless the intended contract deliberately grants a ratifier a separate merge path and both fold and docs state it. Add the exact reviewer-as-merger probe and require target HEAD, receipt ref, and durable projection to remain unchanged on refusal.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers are cmd/gs composition, Workroom interpreter/fold, and their reference documentation. The pure-fold path-lineage narrowing is coherent and docs/reference/architecture.md plus docs/reference/gs/merge.md now honestly state that the fold cannot verify Git head, diff, or tree. But the CLI does not enforce the documented implementation-author boundary before crossing into Git, so the cross-layer contract is incomplete and blocks approval.\n\nSecurity: the repair removes the unrelated-tree privilege escalation by the legitimate implementer. The remaining wrong-signer path is a denial/authority defect: an unrelated participant can consume an approval and mutate the target before their receipt is rejected. No secrets are involved; the exposed boundaries are actor identity, single-use approval authority, Git HEAD, and cross-author retirement. This blocks approval.\n\nSimplification: deriving one implementation-author fingerprint from the already-resolved approval artifact and comparing it once before merge is simpler and safer than relying on the later fold rejection. The lineage helpers otherwise express the narrowed contract directly. No additional simplification blocker found.\n\nVerification at the exact head: go test ./internal/workroom -run 'TestMergeReceipt|TestFreeStandingSupersession' -count=1 passed; focused cmd/gs merge tests for cross-author preflight, citation-preserving succession/orphaning, bare deletion, wider-directory selection, unrelated candidates, sealed retry, exact approval, and no-successor behavior passed; focused internal/docset classification/succeeded-retirement tests passed; go vet ./... and go build ./... passed. The added wrong-merger probe fails only because HEAD moved before the expected refusal, preserving the blocking evidence. Companion artifacts 8c28cb04 at internal/workroom and 0217b3c5 at internal/app are effective, live, non-stale, and name this exact head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:514ab482d8b1f75d277d6b33e73ffdfc428dffdc","head":"a3bf832ef1fd8af73c00d4d9c3783628ab8c2f13","verdict":"changes-requested"}}